<!-- ============ 10 QUALITY ============ -->
<section class="section band-dark" id="sportswear-quality" aria-labelledby="sportswear-quality-title" data-od-id="sw-quality">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label label--onDark">10 / Quality</p>
        <h2 id="sportswear-quality-title">What Gets Checked Before Your Sportswear Ships?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Base checks on the approved sample and order specification. Define important measurements, appearance points, working details, quantities, and packing requirements. Agree any formal inspection method, tolerance, test, or report before production.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="sw-spec">
      <article class="sw-spec-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="sw-spec-num">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Measurements, Fit-Critical Points, and Workmanship</h3>
          <p>Check measurements that control fit and movement across relevant sizes. Review seams, loose or skipped stitches, puckering, stress points, panel alignment, and symmetry. Acceptance rules and tolerances must come from the approved order specification.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="sw-spec-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="sw-spec-num">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Stretch Areas, Openings, Pockets, and Trims</h3>
          <p>Review waistbands, cuffs, openings, zippers, drawcords, pockets, gussets, and other working parts. Check attachment, operation, position, and appearance. Any performance test remains separate and follows the method and target agreed for the project.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="sw-spec-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="sw-spec-num">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Color, Decoration, Labels, and Order Identity</h3>
          <p>Compare colors, artwork, numbers, names, placements, labels, and trims with approved references. Match teamwear variations to the order list. Check care and size information, barcode or sticker data, and attachment position before packing.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="sw-spec-row" data-reveal>
        <span class="sw-spec-num">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Quantities, Assortments, Cartons, and Handoff Records</h3>
          <p>Verify quantities, size and color assortments, individual packing, carton contents, and carton marks against the order. Provide agreed inspection or packing information at the correct stage so the buyer can connect packed goods with the approved product.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="sw-media" data-reveal>
      <div class="sw-ph" role="img" aria-label="Pending image slot for verified sportswear measurement and workmanship checks">
