<!-- ============ 11 FAQ ============ -->
<section class="section band-alt" id="sportswear-faq" aria-labelledby="sportswear-faq-title" data-od-id="sw-faq">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="pd-head">
      <div class="pd-title" data-reveal>
        <p class="label">11 / FAQ</p>
        <h2 id="sportswear-faq-title">Questions Buyers Ask Before Ordering Custom Sportswear</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pd-note" data-reveal>
        <p class="lead">Use these questions to clarify the product before sampling and to separate project requirements from unverified performance or commercial assumptions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary><span class="pd-faq-num">01</span><h3>Can We Start With a Photo or Reference Garment?</h3></summary>
        <p>Yes. A photo, physical reference, or concept can start the review but does not replace the final specification. Add intended changes, measurements, fabric, artwork, quantity, labels, and packing. Sampling creates the reviewable product reference.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="pd-faq-num">02</span><h3>Which Fabric Should We Choose for Our First Style?</h3></summary>
        <p>Begin with the garment, activity, fit, climate, hand feel, stretch, opacity, and decoration. Then compare candidate fabrics by composition, structure, weight, color, and project-specific performance requirements.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="pd-faq-num">03</span><h3>Can We Request Moisture-Wicking, Quick-Dry, UPF, or Water Resistance?</h3></summary>
        <p>Include the target, intended claim, market, test method, and acceptance value. Testing and supporting documents must be confirmed for the selected material and order. Generic sportswear wording is not evidence.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="pd-faq-num">04</span><h3>What Is the MOQ and How Long Will Sampling Take?</h3></summary>
        <p>Both depend on the product and order. Styles, quantity splits, fabric, custom components, decoration, personalization, packing, and revisions affect the answer. Share the brief to confirm MOQ, sample cost, revision terms, and timing.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><span class="pd-faq-num">05</span><h3>What Can We Review During Production and Packing?</h3></summary>
        <p>Buyers can request stage-linked photos, measurements, inspection information, packing details, or related documents. Agree the record, timing, and purpose before production. Unstructured images do not prove every requirement.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

